  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569959.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "PSMEM (Puget Sound Marine Environmental Modeling)",
  "description": "The Puget Sound Marine Environmental Modeling (PSMEM) is a project of a partnership of five separate organizations, collectively operating or developing four dynamic, predictive models of the Puget Sound's aquatic environment and one biogeochemistry module. Each model has a different spatial coverage with a goal to integrate the modeling efforts into a coordinated whole.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To develop quantitative understanding of Puget Sound's circulation and marine ecosystem, and of the sensitivity of the physical and the biological system to natural and human perturbations; and to develop models of the Sound that can aid agencies with responsibilities for environmental management in making informed decisions and serve as marine science education tools.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569960",
